PROJECT PROPOSAL

Hospital Patient Management Dashboard Using Python and Power BI

1. Introduction

The Hospital Patient Management Dashboard is a data analytics and visualization project developed using Python, Google Colab, and Microsoft Power BI. The project focuses on analyzing hospital patient data collected from the Kaggle platform to generate meaningful insights into hospital operations and patient-related information.

The project involves various stages, including data collection, data cleaning, preprocessing, exploratory data analysis (EDA), data visualization, and dashboard development.

Python is used for data cleaning, preprocessing, and analysis, while Google Colab provides an interactive environment for executing Python code and performing data visualization. Microsoft Power BI is used to develop an interactive dashboard that presents important hospital statistics through charts, graphs, and KPI indicators.

The dashboard helps users understand patient demographics, admission patterns, department-wise patient distribution, billing information, and other relevant hospital-related insights.

2. Problem Statement

Hospitals generate large amounts of patient-related data, which may contain missing values, duplicate records, inconsistent formats, and other data quality issues. Analyzing such raw data manually can be time-consuming and may make it difficult to identify meaningful patterns and trends.

To address this problem, this project aims to collect hospital patient data from Kaggle, clean and preprocess it using Python, perform exploratory data analysis using Google Colab, and develop an interactive dashboard using Microsoft Power BI.

The proposed system transforms raw hospital data into structured information and meaningful visual insights, supporting better understanding of hospital operations and data-driven decision-making.

3. Objectives

- To collect a hospital patient dataset from the Kaggle platform.
- To understand the structure and attributes of the collected dataset.
- To clean and preprocess raw data using Python.
- To identify and handle missing values, duplicate records, and inconsistent data.
- To perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) using Python in Google Colab.
- To analyze patient demographics and admission-related information.
- To identify department-wise patient distribution and billing patterns.
- To create meaningful charts and visualizations using Python.
- To develop an interactive hospital management dashboard using Power BI.
- To generate meaningful insights through KPIs, charts, and interactive filters.

4. Project Methodology

The project is implemented through the following phases:

Phase 1: Data Collection

- Collect the hospital patient dataset from Kaggle.
- Download the dataset in CSV format.
- Understand the dataset structure, columns, and data types.
- Identify relevant attributes required for analysis.

Phase 2: Data Cleaning and Preprocessing Using Python

Python libraries such as Pandas and NumPy are used for data cleaning and preprocessing.

The following operations are performed:

- Load the raw dataset using Pandas.
- Check dataset dimensions and column information.
- Identify and handle missing and null values.
- Detect and remove duplicate records.
- Correct inconsistent data formats.
- Convert columns into appropriate data types.
- Handle invalid or irrelevant records.
- Standardize column names and categorical values.
- Save the cleaned dataset for further analysis.

Phase 3: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) Using Google Colab

Google Colab is used as the development environment to execute Python code and perform exploratory data analysis.

The analysis includes:

- Total number of patient records.
- Patient demographic analysis.
- Age-wise patient distribution.
- Gender-wise patient distribution.
- Department-wise patient analysis.
- Admission and discharge pattern analysis, wherever date fields are available.
- Billing amount and revenue analysis, wherever billing information is available.
- Identification of important patterns and trends in the dataset.

Phase 4: Data Visualization Using Python

Python visualization libraries such as Matplotlib and Seaborn are used to represent analytical results graphically.

The visualizations include:

- Bar charts for categorical comparisons.
- Pie charts for distribution analysis.
- Histograms for numerical data distribution.
- Count plots for category-wise patient analysis.
- Box plots for identifying outliers.
- Heatmaps for understanding correlations.
- Other relevant graphs based on dataset attributes.

Phase 5: Dashboard Development Using Microsoft Power BI

The cleaned dataset is imported into Microsoft Power BI to create an interactive hospital patient management dashboard.

The dashboard includes relevant visualizations such as:

- KPI Cards: Total Patients, Average Age, Total Billing Amount, and other available key metrics.
- Donut Charts: Gender Distribution and Patient Category Distribution.
- Bar Charts: Department-wise Patient Distribution.
- Line Charts: Admission Trends over Time, if date information is available.
- Column Charts: Age Group Analysis.
- Pie Charts: Patient Category and Status Distribution.
- Treemaps: Department-wise Patient Distribution.
- Slicers: Department, Gender, Age Group, and other relevant dataset attributes.

The final dashboard is designed with interactive filters, consistent formatting, and meaningful visual representations to make data exploration easier.

5. Proposed System

The proposed system uses Python, Google Colab, and Microsoft Power BI to analyze and visualize hospital patient data.

Initially, the dataset is collected from Kaggle and processed using Python. Data cleaning and preprocessing techniques are applied to improve data quality and reliability.

After preprocessing, Exploratory Data Analysis is performed in Google Colab to identify important patterns, trends, and relationships in the dataset. Python visualization libraries are also used to represent the analytical results.

The cleaned dataset is then imported into Power BI, where an interactive dashboard is developed using KPI cards, charts, graphs, and slicers.

The proposed system provides a structured approach to hospital data analysis and transforms raw patient records into meaningful visual insights.

